            <ArticleTitle>Imaging patterns with 99mTc-PIPIDA in evaluating abdominal pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1386-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A random retrospective review of hepatobiliary scans on 86 adult patients with abdominal pain revealed four distinct imaging patterns: normal, cystic duct obstruction, obstructive, and sick liver pattern. A normal pattern was found to exclude acute cholecystitis and was the pattern most frequently observed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
